  "body": "Asymptotes   Complete the table for the functions What is true about the -values at ?                                         Plot the points from the table and connect them with smooth curves.    As increases through larger and larger values, what happens to the values of ?  What happens to as decreases through larger and larger negative values (that is, for ...)?  Will the graph of ever touch the -axis? Why or why not?  Repeat part(c) for the graph of .  Next we'll examine the graphs near . Evaluate for several -values close to zero and complete the table below. What happens to the values of as approaches zero?                                  Extend your graph to reflect your answer. Will the graph ever touch the -axis? Why or why not?  Repeat part (d) for the graph of .                                  State the intervals on which each graph is increasing. Write a few sentences comparing the two graphs.  Here is our first encounter with asymptotes. It may be helpful to graph a few translations of and with technology, e.g. and , to show that asymptotes do not always coincide with the axes.   "
